      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "His preference for consensus-building doesn't necessarily mean he will be slow; instead, it could prevent critical errors that cost the team money later. By focusing on long-term planning, Marcus might actually be the only one capable of navigating our \"fast and break things\" spirit with enough foresight to avoid costly failures. I suggest framing his structured approach as his unique ability to build momentum on a foundation of stability, turning potential hesitation into strategic strength. Ultimately, this perspective might convince him to adapt while reassessing whether the high-pressure environment truly suits his natural working style.",
